# OpenDesk local environment defaults
#
# Usage
#   1. Copy this file to .opendesk.env in the directory where you run OpenDesk:
#        cp .opendesk.env.example .opendesk.env
#   2. Select a profile below, then run your usual command without adding
#      terminal-output flags:
#        ./opendesk -script script.js
#   3. Keep .opendesk.env local. It is ignored by Git.
#
# What this replaces
#   These values are defaults for the matching CLI options. For example,
#   OPENDESK_CONSOLE_MODE=full behaves like adding -console-mode full to every
#   invocation from this directory. A CLI option still wins for one command:
#        ./opendesk -script script.js -console-mode normal
#
# Resolution order (lowest to highest)
#   built-in normal -> .env -> .opendesk.env -> exported OPENDESK_CONSOLE_*
#   -> explicit CLI flags
#
# Supported parameter: OPENDESK_CONSOLE_MODE
#   normal  Script log/info/warn/error and completion summary; no debug. Default.
#   script  All script logs, including console.debug and console.time*.
#   full    Script, framework, metadata, summary and error diagnostics.
#   meta    Execution source/hash/lifecycle metadata and errors only.
#   summary Completion summary and errors only.
#   quiet   Errors only.
#   agent   Agent JSON summary; -output-format json also selects this profile.
OPENDESK_CONSOLE_MODE=normal

# Optional parameter: OPENDESK_CONSOLE_CATEGORIES
# This exact list replaces the selected mode's categories. Allowed values are
# framework, meta, script, summary and error. Leave it commented out to use
# the mode above. Examples:
# OPENDESK_CONSOLE_CATEGORIES=script,summary,error
# OPENDESK_CONSOLE_CATEGORIES=framework,script,summary,error
#
# Runtime variables may also be declared here and are exposed to trusted local
# scripts through the frozen Execution.env snapshot. They are not automatic
# CLI flags, are never shell-expanded, and are overridden by variables already
# present when the OpenDesk process starts. HTTP/MCP/Scheduler executions do
# not inherit that host environment. Do not commit secrets in this template.
# MY_PROJECT_MODE=development
